//// Decision 215 — `==` / `!=` between an `f64` and an integer literal is
//// refused at the literal: the comparison is exact (decision B2, which used
//// to answer `2.0 == 2` with `false`) and the literal's widening to `f64`
//// (decision 209) would read it two ways. Write the float.

pub fn main() {
    val x = 2.0;
    @print(x == 2);
}
